        <div class="tracker__section dash__today">
      <h2 class="tracker__section-title">Top AI Stories Today</h2>
              <div class="dash__today-story">
          <h3 class="dash__today-headline">
                          <a href="https://x.com/kimi_moonshot/status/2078855608565207130" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Moonshot pauses Kimi K3 subscriptions as GPUs hit capacity</a>
                      </h3>
          <p class="dash__today-summary">Moonshot posted on X on July 19 that Kimi K3 &#039;received far more love than we expected, and our GPUs are feeling it,&#039; with demand over the past 48 hours pushing close to capacity. To protect existing subscribers, the lab is temporarily pausing new subscriptions while it adds GPU capacity, and plan…</p>          <div class="dash__today-meta">
            <a href="https://x.com/kimi_moonshot/status/2078855608565207130" target="_blank" rel="noopener">x.com</a>
            · 4h ago · Builders                      </div>
        </div>
              <div class="dash__today-story">
          <h3 class="dash__today-headline">
                          <a href="https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/07/18/world/chinas-kimi-k3-rattles-us-ai-industry/2386827" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sacks warns Kimi K3 shows US losing the AI race</a>
                      </h3>
          <p class="dash__today-summary">White House AI advisor David Sacks called Moonshot&#039;s Kimi K3 release &#039;concerning&#039; and said &#039;This is how you lose the AI race. Permissionless innovation is how America won,&#039; blaming US data center blocks, state regulations, and federal pre-approval requirements.</p>          <div class="dash__today-meta">
            <a href="https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/07/18/world/chinas-kimi-k3-rattles-us-ai-industry/2386827" target="_blank" rel="noopener">manilatimes.net</a>
            · 19h ago · Geopolitics                      </div>
        </div>
              <div class="dash__today-story">
          <h3 class="dash__today-headline">
                          <a href="/alerts/anthropic-openai-staff-outdonate-prior-big-tech-cohorts">OpenAI and Anthropic staff outspend Google, Meta on politics</a>
                      </h3>
          <p class="dash__today-summary">SF Standard analysis: Anthropic employees have donated $3.83M and OpenAI staff $876K to federal campaigns this cycle (excluding Brockman&#039;s $25M super-PAC gifts), already outpacing Google ($670K), Facebook ($1.08M) and Airbnb ($747K) at the same post-IPO stage. Roughly 59 of every 1,000 Anthropic …</p>          <div class="dash__today-meta">
            <a href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/07/18/ai-s-new-political-donor-class-already-outspending-big-tech-s-last-one/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">sfstandard.com</a>
            · 17h ago · Law             · <a href="/alerts/anthropic-openai-staff-outdonate-prior-big-tech-cohorts" class="dash__today-brief">our brief →</a>          </div>
        </div>
              <div class="dash__today-story">
          <h3 class="dash__today-headline">
                          <a href="https://x.com/Alibaba_Qwen/status/2078759124914098291" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Qwen 3.8 to launch open-weight, Alibaba claims only Fable 5 beats it</a>
                      </h3>
          <p class="dash__today-summary">Alibaba&#039;s Qwen team posted July 19 that Qwen 3.8 is &#039;launching and going open-weight soon&#039; at 2.4 trillion parameters, positioning it as second only to Anthropic&#039;s Fable 5 among frontier models. The Qwen3.8-Max-Preview is already live on Qwen Cloud alongside the announcement, extending Alibaba&#039;s …</p>          <div class="dash__today-meta">
            <a href="https://x.com/Alibaba_Qwen/status/2078759124914098291" target="_blank" rel="noopener">x.com</a>
            · 11h ago · Builders                      </div>
        </div>
              <div class="dash__today-story">
          <h3 class="dash__today-headline">
                          <a href="/node/7279">AI advice tanks accuracy from 27% to 9%, but confidence soars</a>
                      </h3>
          <p class="dash__today-summary">A study by Valerio Capraro (Milano-Bicocca), Chiara Marcoccia (ENS) and Walter Quattrociocchi (Sapienza) using Step 3.5 Flash finds AI advice drops user accuracy from 27% to 9% and &#039;I don&#039;t know&#039; responses from 44% to 3%, while confidence climbs from 30% to 76%. Wharton is cited putting the &#039;cogn…</p>          <div class="dash__today-meta">
            <a href="https://thenextweb.com/news/ai-advice-suppresses-critical-thinking-wrong-answers-study" target="_blank" rel="noopener">thenextweb.com</a>
            · 0m ago · Research             · <a href="/node/7279" class="dash__today-brief">our brief →</a>          </div>
        </div>
          </div>
  
