                                      <a href="https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/models" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Kimi K3 gets Standard and High reasoning tiers alongside Max</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">Two days after debuting the 2.8T-parameter Kimi K3 with max-only reasoning, Moonshot updated its Kimi Code documentation on July 18 to expose three reasoning_effort tiers — low, high (now the default) and max — letting developers trade off compute against latency. Kimi K3&#039;s original release blog explicitly deferred low- and high-effort modes to &#039;subsequent updates,&#039; which have now landed in the Kimi Code environment; the main Kimi API quickstart still notes max-only, with additional levels &#039;coming soon.&#039;</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story" data-beat="research">
