            </div>
                                      <a href="https://tensorlabbet.com/2026/07/19/medqaswe_post_training/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Small open models post-trained to pass Swedish medical exam</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">A new blog post from tensorlabbet documents post-training experiments on the MedQA-SWE benchmark: MedGemma-1.5-4B jumped from 14.6% to 60.8% accuracy via LoRA supervised fine-tuning that fixed formatting failures, while Qwen3.5-4B reached 86.7% via RLVR-style reinforcement learning with early-exit reasoning interventions. The results argue that small open-weight models can now match frontier performance on Swedish medical licensing questions through targeted post-training rather than scale alone.</div>          </div>
