                                      <a href="/alerts/sebastian-rucci-pushes-10b-imperial-valley-ai-data-center" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Ex-strip-club operator pushes California&#039;s biggest data center</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">WSJ profiles Sebastian Rucci, a Huntington Beach lawyer whose past ventures faced legal probes, as he pushes ahead with a $10B, 330MW AI/HPC campus in Imperial County — poised to become California&#039;s largest data center. Project requires 750,000 gallons of water/day, has drawn heavy local backlash, and is openly seeking to avoid California Environmental Quality Act review. Rucci has purchased 235 acres and targets summer 2028 for first operations.</div>          </div>
