                                      <a href="/alerts/wsj-uae-wins-ai-chip-access-g42-to-reincorporate-as-us-firm" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">WSJ: CIA officer spied on G42 to unlock UAE AI chip access</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">Wall Street Journal reports CIA operative Jonny Gannon ran an intelligence operation targeting UAE AI firm G42 to probe its China ties, ultimately helping the Gulf state gain expanded US AI chip access by allaying US national-security suspicions. G42, controlled by UAE NSA Sheikh Tahnoon bin Zayed, plans to reincorporate as a US company primarily owned by US investors. Story lands weeks after Commerce eased chip export controls on UAE.</div>          </div>
