                                      <a href="/alerts/ztes-nubia-bills-navix-ultra-as-first-agentic-ai-phone" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Nubia&#039;s NaviX Ultra swaps the home screen for ByteDance&#039;s Doubao agent</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">ZTE-owned Nubia used WAIC 2026 in Shanghai to unveil the NaviX Ultra, which it and Bloomberg are billing as the world&#039;s first agentic AI smartphone — a device with no traditional home screen or app grid, built entirely around ByteDance&#039;s Doubao voice agent triggered by a dedicated orange side button. The phone won a 2026 SAIL award ahead of the conference and shipped in blue, black, pink and white variants; Nubia is preparing mass production while full specs and pricing follow. It joins a broader Chinese OEM push to reimagine the phone as an agent shell rather than a launcher for apps.</div>          </div>
