                                      <a href="/alerts/white-house-now-vets-who-gets-openai-anthropic-frontier-models" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">White House now controls who gets access to frontier AI models</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">CNBC reports the Trump administration is now dictating which partners can access frontier AI models from OpenAI and Anthropic, extending oversight beyond the newly launched Gold Eagle cyber clearinghouse into distribution decisions previously held by the labs themselves. Anthropic&#039;s Project Glasswing (for Mythos cybersecurity model) and OpenAI&#039;s Daybreak partner rosters will now require explicit government approval before adding customers. A White House official said engagement is &#039;voluntary,&#039; yet the administration blocked Claude Mythos 5 and Fable 5 in June over national-security concerns and only reinstated access after weeks of negotiations with Anthropic; OpenAI&#039;s GPT-5.6 Sol was similarly gated to Trump-approved customers at launch.</div>          </div>
