              <span class="dash__story-time">2d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">32</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="/node/7127" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Japan bets $6B on 27,500 Nvidia Rubin GPUs for sovereign robot AI</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">Japan&#039;s newly formed Noetra Corp — a consortium of ~44 companies led by SoftBank, Sony, Honda, NEC and Toyota-backed Preferred Networks — will deploy 27,500 Nvidia Rubin GPUs and 13,750 Vera CPUs (382 NVL72 racks, 140MW) as the compute layer for METI&#039;s FRONTia Project, targeting sovereign multimodal foundation models for physical AI and robotics. Tokyo has committed ¥387.3B ($2.4B) through March 2027 within a ¥1T ($6B) five-year package; construction begins 2027 with operations targeted for June 2028. President Hironobu Tamba framed the effort as &#039;a genuine third option&#039; beyond US and Chinese AI stacks, with Japan aiming for 30%+ of a ¥60T global robotics market by 2040.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="compute">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source">huaweicentral.com</span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">2d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">30</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="https://www.huaweicentral.com/huawei-atlas-950-superpod/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Huawei Atlas 950 SuperPoD claims 6.7x Nvidia NVL144 compute</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">At WAIC&#039;s July 16 opening in Shanghai, Huawei publicly unveiled its Atlas 950 SuperPoD, linking 1,024 Ascend chips in a base configuration that scales to 8,192 NPUs, delivering 1 EFLOPS FP8 and 2 EFLOPS FP4 with 256 TB unified memory across 160 cabinets. Huawei claims 6.7x the compute and 15x the memory of Nvidia&#039;s NVL144, using its proprietary Lingqu interconnect at 3µs latency. Availability is targeted for Q4 2026, positioning Huawei&#039;s domestic AI-supernode stack as a Nvidia alternative amid US export restrictions.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="geopolitics">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source">english.news.cn</span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">2d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">29</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="https://english.news.cn/20260717/893fe11097db460ea31b98f131e34ef0/c.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Xi&#039;s WAIC keynote pledges 5,000 AI training slots for Global South</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">In his first-ever keynote at the World AI Conference in Shanghai on July 17, Xi Jinping pledged 5,000 AI training opportunities for developing countries over five years, extended the AI-powered MAZU meteorological warning system to 30 countries, and committed to building AI cooperation centers with ASEAN, the African Union, the Arab League, CELAC, the SCO and BRICS. Xi framed unequal AI access as risking &#039;new historical injustice&#039; and formally established the World AI Cooperation Organization (WAICO) as a counterweight to US-led AI governance.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="workforce">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source">abc7news.com</span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">3d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">28</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="https://abc7news.com/post/4500-google-employees-sign-petition-demanding-layoff-protections/19522280/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Google workers deliver 4,500-signature layoff-protection petition to Pichai</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">Alphabet Workers Union president Parul Koul and about 100 employees rallied at Google&#039;s Mountain View HQ on July 17 to hand a 4,500-signature petition to Sundar Pichai and three other top executives, demanding guaranteed severance, voluntary buyouts before mandatory layoffs, severance-as-extended-paid-leave, and an end to quota-based performance ratings. Koul called it the largest employee feedback effort on job security at Google and framed continued cuts as prioritizing profits over workers while the company&#039;s valuation quadrupled to about $4 trillion. The push comes as CFO Anat Ashkenazi has named AI as a key expansion area and Google keeps trimming Cloud and management headcount.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="field">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source"><a href="https://huggingface.co/blog/security-incident-july-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:inherit;">huggingface.co</a></span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">3d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">33</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="/alerts/hugging-face-discloses-ai-agent-driven-breach-of-internal-clusters" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Hugging Face reveals AI-agent-driven breach of its data pipeline</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">Hugging Face disclosed an autonomous-agent intrusion where a malicious dataset exploited two code-execution paths — a remote-code dataset loader and template injection in dataset config — on a processing worker, then escalated to node access and moved laterally to harvest cloud and cluster credentials. Public models, datasets and Spaces were not tampered with, but internal datasets and service credentials were compromised; users are being told to rotate access tokens. HF used open-weight GLM 5.2 to forensically analyze more than 17,000 attack events after commercial APIs refused to process the exploit payloads.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="builders">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source">kimi.com</span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">3d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">32</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="https://www.kimi.com/blog/kimi-k3" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Moonshot launches Kimi K3, first open 3T-class model with 1M context</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">Moonshot AI officially released Kimi K3 today, a 2.8-trillion-parameter Mixture-of-Experts model with a 1-million-token context window built on the lab&#039;s Kimi Delta Attention plus Attention Residuals architecture, and with native vision baked into the model rather than bolted on. Moonshot claims frontier-adjacent benchmarks (88.3 on Terminal Bench 2.1, 81.2 on FrontierSWE, 93.5 on GPQA-Diamond, 94.3 on MathVision), and a ~2.5x scaling-efficiency gain over K2. The model is live now via the Kimi app, Kimi Work, Kimi Code and the Kimi API, with full open-source weights slated to drop by July 27, making it the largest open model ever released.</div>          </div>
