            </div>
                                      <a href="https://english.news.cn/20260716/2fb3c068a5ec4efbbeb6a88acf155175/c.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">29 nations sign agreement in Shanghai to found China-led WAICO</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">Twenty-nine countries signed an agreement in Shanghai on July 16 to establish the World Artificial Intelligence Cooperation Organization (WAICO), an independent intergovernmental body to be headquartered in Shanghai. Founding signatories include Russia, Belarus, Serbia, Cuba, Brazil, Venezuela, Pakistan, Kazakhstan, Indonesia and Laos, plus 10 African and 12 Asian countries; Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi signed for China and UN Secretary-General António Guterres attended. The signing sets up Xi Jinping&#039;s July 17 WAIC keynote and positions WAICO as a Global-South-tilted counterweight to Western-led AI governance forums.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="robotics">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source"><a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/japans-robotics-and-manufacturing-leaders-build-on-nvidia-cosmos-to-advance-physical-ai-frontier" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:inherit;">nvidianews.nvidia.com</a></span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">3d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">30</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="/node/6845" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Nvidia ships 4B Cosmos 3 Edge world model, 22 Japan robotics giants sign on</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">NVIDIA introduced Cosmos 3 Edge, a 4B-parameter Nemotron-based world model that runs on-device for vision reasoning and robot policy generation across Jetson (including new T2000/T3000 modules), RTX GPUs and DGX systems, with developers able to adapt it to a specific robot, vehicle or sensor in about a day. Alongside, 22 Japanese robotics and manufacturing leaders — AIRoA, Classmethod, Enactic, FANUC, Fujitsu, GROOVE X, Hitachi, Honda R&amp;D, Kawasaki Heavy Industries, Kubota, Mitsui, Mitsubishi, Mujin, NEC, Preferred Networks, SoftBank, Sony, Telexistence, TIER IV, TRON, Turing and Yaskawa — announced they will join the NVIDIA Cosmos Coalition to co-build open physical AI foundation models. New Metropolis libraries claim to speed vision AI system development at least 6x.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="compute">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source">finance.yahoo.com</span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">3d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">36</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/taiwan-chipmaker-tsmc-invest-another-065311994.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">TSMC pledges $100B more for Arizona, hikes 2026 capex to $60-64B</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">TSMC used its July 16 Q2 earnings call to unveil an additional $100B Arizona investment — pushing its total US pledge to $265B across 10 fabs and two packaging facilities — while raising 2026 capex to $60-64B (from $52-56B) and full-year revenue growth guidance to slightly above 40% in USD (from 30%+). Q2 net profit hit a record NT$706.6B ($22B), up 77.4% YoY, and Chairman C.C. Wei said conviction in the multi-year AI megatrend &#039;remains very high.&#039; The Arizona expansion, framed as the largest foreign direct investment in US history, follows the new US-Taiwan trade deal that cut tariffs on Taiwanese goods to 15%.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="law">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source">cryptobriefing.com</span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">4d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">28</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="https://cryptobriefing.com/xai-sues-terry-harwood-grok-deepfakes-minors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">xAI sues Grok user for generating CSAM in first-of-its-kind case</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">xAI filed suit July 14 in federal court in Texas against Terry Harwood, a South Carolina man already facing criminal charges from a February 2026 arrest for sexually exploiting minors, alleging he uploaded non-sexual photos to Grok and bypassed safety protections to generate explicit deepfakes of minors. It&#039;s one of the first cases where an AI company has gone on legal offense against its own user for CSAM generation. xAI disclosed it suspended 52,222 accounts in 2026 and filed 73,604 reports with NCMEC, resulting in at least 244 arrests; it is seeking unspecified damages and a permanent ban.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="compute">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source">fool.com</span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">4d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">31</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/07/15/elon-musk-discreetly-bought-a-1-billion-gas-turbine-company-to-power-ai-heres-what-it-means-for-spacex-investors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Musk secretly bought a $1B gas-turbine firm to power xAI&#039;s Colossus 2</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">An FTC early-termination filing dated May 14, 2026 that surfaced this week shows SpaceX quietly acquired Jacksonville-based APR Energy for roughly $1 billion, giving Musk direct ownership of a fleet of mobile natural-gas and diesel turbines with over 1 GW of capacity. The turbines are the same class powering xAI&#039;s Colossus and Colossus 2 Memphis-area supercomputers that train Grok, and follow last week&#039;s reporting that xAI installed 59 unpermitted turbines near Southaven. The deal underscores that Musk-controlled AI compute is now vertically integrated with its own off-grid power supply, even as Musk publicly champions solar.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="geopolitics">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/15/apple-intelligence-approved-for-launch-in-china-with-alibabas-qwen-ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:inherit;">techcrunch.com</a></span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">4d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">31</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="/alerts/apple-intelligence-cleared-for-china-launch-on-alibabas-qwen" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">Apple Intelligence cleared for China with Alibaba&#039;s Qwen powering it</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">China&#039;s Cyberspace Administration on July 15 registered Apple Intelligence for use in mainland China with Alibaba&#039;s Qwen as the underlying model, clearing the last major regulatory hurdle for Apple&#039;s generative AI features on iPhones sold in Greater China. Alibaba&#039;s US-listed shares rose about 4% on the news. Apple had reportedly evaluated Baidu, DeepSeek and ByteDance before settling on Qwen; the model will power Apple Intelligence across iOS, iPadOS, macOS and visionOS for Chinese users, including text and image generation.</div>          </div>
                  <div class="dash__story dash__story--alert" data-beat="field">
            <div class="dash__story-meta">
                            <span class="dash__story-source"><a href="https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/07/15/1140514/meet-gpt-red-an-llm-super-hacker-openai-built-to-make-its-models-safer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:inherit;">technologyreview.com</a></span>
              <span class="dash__story-time">4d ago</span>
              <span class="dash__alert-badge">ALERT</span>              <span class="dash__story-score">30</span>
            </div>
                                      <a href="/alerts/openais-gpt-red-slashes-prompt-injection-success-on-gpt-56" rel="noopener" class="dash__story-headline">OpenAI&#039;s GPT-Red cuts prompt-injection attacks on GPT-5.6 from 90% to 23%</a>
                        <div class="dash__story-sum">OpenAI unveiled GPT-Red, an internal automated red-teaming LLM used to adversarially train GPT-5.6 against prompt injection: attacks that succeeded 90%+ of the time on GPT-5 now work under 23% on GPT-5.6, and the tool hits 84% attack success vs 13% for human red-teamers on a 2025 benchmark. GPT-Red discovered a previously unknown &#039;fake chain of thought&#039; injection class and even compromised a vending-machine agent in testing, per OpenAI researcher Dylan Hunn. OpenAI says it will not release the model publicly, citing the compute required to reproduce it, and notes it still struggles with multi-turn and image-based attacks.</div>          </div>
              </div>
    </div>

